# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnpm-store
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local editor / agent settings (shared rules stay tracked)
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.codex/hooks.json
/.cursor/hooks.json
/.idea
/.vscode

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# user-uploaded product images (local dev storage)
/public/uploads

# NOTE: /drizzle is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It was, from the `db:push` era when the directory only held throwaway
# snapshots. Migrations are now the schema's record (`docs/BACKEND.md` §0), and
# ignoring them had two consequences worth stating: the migration chain was not
# version controlled at all, and `pnpm check:rls` — whose static pass scans
# `drizzle/*.sql` — found zero files in CI and therefore passed vacuously,
# checking nothing.

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

.env.local
# Local TLS for `pnpm dev:https` — contains a PRIVATE KEY. Never commit.
certs/

# Scratch output from test runs redirected to a file (`pnpm test:integration > x.log`).
# One of these was committed once; ignoring the pattern is cheaper than remembering.
*.log
